Z||000000||Mach10||07-07-2001||05:49 PM||||My car started overheating again, and I checked the reservoir. Almost empty. <BR>!#$%!#$!!! I topped it off 4 weeks ago. So, it looks like I'm loosing 2-3L per month. Slow leak? I don't get any spots on the driveway, or in parking lots. My exhaust doesn't smoke. I am at a loss. The only clue I may have is that my rad cap hisses when warm, and to be honest, doesn't seem to fit as nice as on my other cars. Thoughts?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-07-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||07-07-2001||05:56 PM||||Well the first easy thing to do is yes change your radiator cap.they do ware out over time and do leak.I also would highly recomend having someone or place do a preasure test for you to see if you have a leak some where else. hope this helps ||||reg||4
Z||000002||theogre||07-07-2001||06:12 PM||||The correct Stant part number for the new cap is in my cave.... I'd change that first.<P>While it's off,,, carefully check the filler neck and and the overflow stuff. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||07-07-2001||06:42 PM||||Thanks Ogre. Do you actually follow me around? You always post to me when my car overheats!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I like that.||||reg||6
Z||000004||Mach10||07-09-2001||03:29 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Well, I found the leak. Looks like the waterpump. #$^#%, #$%#$,!@@#$, #$%#$.<BR>The damn thing starts blowing fluid when the revs go up. Now I have to pull the damn thing apart. *sigh*<P>Apart from the awkward angle, are there any other problems I can expect? Horror stories anyone? I'm hoping that once I get it on stands and have a look that it's just a hose... <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000005||JasonS||07-09-2001||08:29 AM||||My '84 had a slow leak and would overheat about once a month.  I never could see where it was leaking at.  I finally went to discount and  got some alumiseal leak stop stuff.  Worked like a charm.  No more leaks.  I suggest doing that first before spending a whole lot of money.||||reg||14
Z||000006||Mach10||07-10-2001||01:14 PM||||I've used that stop-leak stuff before. All it did was clog my heater core. I'd rather fix the problem permanently, especially since I'm going on a LONG road trip. I'm 95% sure that the leak is coming from the weep hole in the water pump. Stopping that leak will just hide the fact that my water pump's about to self-destruct. I've bought a pump (39.95 + core  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) and have ear-marked an entire day to get it done. ||||reg||6
